124: 
125: ## 🚀 Python Source Installation & Setup
126: 
127: ### Prerequisites
128: - Python 3.9+ (Python 3.10+ recommended)
129: - Standard pip package manager
130: 
131: ### Setup
132: ```bash
133: # Clone the repository
134: git clone https://github.com/swastik-v1/NTFS-UM-Project-2.git
135: cd NTFS-UM-Project-2
136: 
137: # Install dependencies
138: pip install -r requirements.txt
139: ```
140: 
141: > **Note:** Cryptographic hashing relies on Python's built-in `hashlib` standard library module, requiring zero third-party downloads or external API access.
142: 
143: ---
144: 
145: ## 💻 Usage
146: 
147: ### 1. Launch the Native Windows Desktop App (Default)
148: ```bash
149: python main.py
150: # or
151: python main.py --desktop
152: # or
153: python app_desktop.py
154: ```
155: * Spawns a dedicated native window with the live SPLUNK-style dashboard.
156: * Adds a shield icon to the **Windows System Tray** (near the taskbar clock).
157: * Minimizing or closing the window keeps monitoring active in the background.
158: * Triggers native **Windows Toast Notifications** whenever a suspicious file event occurs.
159: * Clicking any log row opens the **Vertical Incident Report Drawer in chat block form**.
160: 
161: ### 2. Start Headless Monitoring (Console Only)
162: ```bash
163: python main.py --monitor
164: ```
165: 
166: ### 3. Start Monitoring + Browser Dashboard
167: ```bash
168: python main.py --monitor --dashboard
169: # Open http://127.0.0.1:5000 in your browser
170: ```
171: 
172: ### 4. Generate Security Audit Report
173: ```bash
174: python main.py --report
175: ```
176: Compiles a structured report in the `reports/` directory containing summary metrics, policy violation breakdown, and chronological logs.
177: 
178: ### 5. Verify Single File Hash
179: ```bash
180: python main.py --test-hash "path/to/file.docx"
181: ```
